 ## Conclusion
 
-pump.fun is moving from a product entered through a wallet address to a consumer trading account it can operate. Shared sign-in across web and app is the immediate change for users. Perps, multichain support, deposits, retention, and product eligibility could explain the longer-term choice. If pump.fun wants an embedded wallet to sign directly for an existing address, key import is the part of its implementation that most needs independent verification.
+pump.fun is moving from a product entered through a wallet address to an account it can use to serve and retain consumers. Shared sign-in across web and app is the immediate change for users. Perps, multichain support, deposits, retention, and product eligibility could explain the longer-term choice. If pump.fun wants an embedded wallet to sign directly for an existing address, key import is the part of its implementation that most needs independent verification.
 
-**The platform should publish signing permissions, recovery conditions, and a verifiable security audit.** Users who need to migrate can retain independent access via the official export path and keep only trading funds at the migrated address. Larger holdings belong in Phantom or a hardware wallet controlled by a separate key. Ledger and multisig users who still want to use pump.fun can open a separate trading account and keep the original wallet for safekeeping.
+**The platform should publish signing permissions, recovery conditions, and a verifiable security audit.** Users who need to migrate can retain independent access via the official export path and keep only trading funds at the migrated address. For larger holdings, use a separate key in Phantom or a hardware wallet. Ledger and multisig users who still want to use pump.fun can open a separate trading account and keep the original wallet for safekeeping.
